0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T21:13:57-07:00","id":869082,"title":"","content":"There is a Japanese visual novel series called Umineko: When They Cry (by the same author that wrote Higurashi). Umineko is one of the most Changeling-themed stories I've read, right down to the way magic works (it works stronger around people who believe in it, and functions poorly, if at all, against those who disbelieve in magic). If you replace the word witch with changeling, you're all set.<br /> <br /> There is an anime series, but it was of very poor quality. The manga however is worth checking out if you don't have the 60 or so hours to read the visual novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T21:30:53-07:00","id":869094,"title":"","content":"Both of those animes were... disturbing and creepy. They'd be inspiration for very dark games or backgrounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-ant