banal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:54:39-07:00","id":874680,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised no one's mentioned Big Fish or Over the Garden Wall yet. Over the Garden Wall is basically a childling (boggan?) taking his enchanted brother along for a trip through the Near Dreaming.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Vorlon totally mentioned Big Fish in the second post. *facepalm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11658,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","user":"Rabbit Pooka","date":". 04-26-2016, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:25:01-07:00","id":874723,"title":"","content":"Big Fish is my favorite pooka story. I'm surprised I didn't mention it earlier too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T18:05:28-07:00","id":875065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neon.Sidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=874512#post874512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't conceive anything more banal than Harry Potter! I can't even see anything that relates to CtD!<br /> I mean, they're are wizards living in a magical reality that is twice as boring as Earth! They suffer because they can't buy a flying broom, they bully different people at school and they have ridiculously tedious magic classes... I would be very disappointed if someone could turn magic into something so boring and banal.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Neat......</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:14:43-07:00","id":876711,"title":"","content":"All great suggestions! Mine are less appropriate, and more than a little obvious, but they have their uses.<br /> <br /> While a bit more Changeling: The Lost than Changeling: The Dreaming, I do have to point to Hellboy 2: The Golden Army. While a bit campy, in that distinctly Hellboy way, there are some segments (the tomb of the Golden Army, the Goblin Market, and the elemental creature) that make good inspirations for locations in the Near Dreaming and chimera, particularly in a modern setting. Plus, Prince Nuada kind of exemplifies what a Sidhe knight who goes Unseelie out of sheer bitterness and rage might look like.<br /> <br /> While also more The Lost (and, I'm half-convinced, probably a case of the tail wagging the dog to use it as an inspiration for a Changeling game at all), Lost Girl also has some value. Particularly, the way their Seelie and Unseelie equivalents interact, and the way those courts aren't purely good or evil in stereotypical ways, can come in handy for more social games. The character of Kenzi also makes a great example of an Enchanted mortal ally. Some of the monsters they fight can also make decent inspiration for Gallain, rogue chimera, or adhene. As a warning, the show is a bit adult, and some episodes can definitely be a bit monster-of-the-week, but it's a fun fae-focused romp if you don't take it too seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:17:42-07:00","id":878293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=861548#post861548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently nine books strong, Seanan McGuire's <i>October Daye</i> series is pretty much a love letter to the game. Sure, she's renamed a couple of things, thrown in a couple of house rules . . . but the whole series reads like a <i>Changeling</i> campaign. Sidhe nobles ruling hidden freeholds, commoner changelings resisting their rules, lost kingdoms hidden in the depths of the Dreaming . . . the characters even perform bunks to channel their magic. In fact, it would not surprise me in the least to learn that October &amp;quot;Toby&amp;quot; Daye used to be the author's pc in a <i>Changeling</i> game<br /> <br /> The protagonist, Sir October Daye, was a sidhe knight, noted for her street smarts and ability to ferret out secrets. But when her latest quest blows up in her face, she spends the next decade unwillingly exploring new career options . . . as a fish. When she finally escapes the curse, her mortal life is in ruins, and she realizes she's no longer a wilder. As a newly minted grump, she tries to sink into Banality, into forgetfulness . . . Until one day her old life comes calling:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My personal favorite (so far) is book three, <i>An Artificial Night</i>. All across San Francisco, parents wake to find their children gone, stolen from their beds in the night by a Lost One. Initially,Toby has no intention of challenging such a dangerous opponent - she's a sleuth, not a soldier. And then her best friend calls her, sick with worry . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. You weren't kidding. You can practically hear the dice rolling. I'm honestly surprised there wasn't a beef with this considering how little is changed from the game to the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T16:50:05-07:00","id":879093,"title":"","content":"...Family Guy...all the Stewie/Brian adventures could be considered for how outaregous and weird they are","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T06:53:41-07:00","id":879494,"title":"","content":"We can also add Life Is Strange. A unique newer point-and-click adventure game, the entire game is a metaphor for growing up, albeit in a different way than Changeling. While the supernatural elements are a bit more subtle, the game's use of symbolism are pure Dreaming. Plus, it highlights the trials, tribulations, and opportunities of growing up and building interpersonal relationships in the real world while being something more. The game has won and been nominated for a boatload of awards, and deservedly so.<br /> <br /> Also, without spoilers, the nightmare sequence of Episode 5 seems like great fodder for an ST when your players have pissed you off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4732-drazosh","name":"Drazosh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:17:50-07:00","id":896626,"title":"","content":"<b>Sucker Punch</b> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PVJarcI0yhE\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>) looks like a textbook <i>Changeling</i> movie. I haven't had a chance to watch it (yet), but apparently its about a supposedly mad girl fighting across multiple fantasy worlds for a chance at freedom. <br /> <br /> The original edition of <i>Changeling</i> cited <b>Mythago Wood</b> as a key inspiration. The dynamic isn't <i>quite </i>the same, but the story of a man chasing his dream girl (and evil brother) through a forest populated by beings out of myth and legend could easily be adapted to <i>C:tD</i>. And &quot;Hellfire Harry&quot; provides an excellent example of how new fae come about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mystery of Ryhope Wood, Britain's last fragment of primeval forest, consumed George Huxley's entire long life. Now, after his death, his sons have taken up his work. But what they discover is numinous and perilous beyond all expectation.<br /> <br /> For the Wood, larger inside than out, is a labyrinth full of myths come to life, &quot;mythagos&quot; that can change you forever. A labyrinth where love and beauty haunt your dreams. . .and may drive you insane. </div> </div> </div>Oh, and Susan Cooper's &quot;Dark is Rising&quot; quintet works very, very well as Changeling story. Particularly after you get past the first book (<i>Over Sea, Under Stone</i>), and the series introduces Bran and Will. Its all Arthurian (while a <i>Changeling</i> campaign can be more . . . mixed), but still very, very good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will Stanton\u2019s ordinary life is shattered with the dreadful revelation that the Dark\u2014the source of all evil\u2014is rising in its last and greatest bid to control the world. He finds that he is no ordinary boy, but the last-born of the Old Ones, immortals dedicated to keeping mankind free from the Dark. Soon Will is swept up in the great battle, along with his ageless master, Merriman; the three Drew children, who are mortal but have their own vital part to play; and a strange boy named Bran. These six fight fear and death in a quest through time and space interwoven with the most ancient myths of the islands of Britain\u2014until, at last, Will and Bran find the weapon that will ultimately vanquish the Dark. </div> </div> </div>Or if you want something a bit more obscure, try the live action <b>Witchblade</b> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gRJa9hqJHeY\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>) series. Its not hard to see the titular artifact as an Inanimae (<i>a la</i> a Selkie's coat), and the show blurs the lines between reality and fantasy, madness and sanity, in much the same way <i>Changeling</i> does. Take special note of the fight scenes - there are some <i>really</i> wild ideas that you can borrow for your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T15:25:40-07:00","id":897257,"title":"","content":"The Eccentric Family. Its an anime about a family of tanuki and the fantastical magical world that lives just under the surface that no moral ever sees. while its not one for one Changeling the family have a pretty good set up for many a Pooka, the Professor is wonderful Inspiration for a Grump who's on his downward spiral, Benten works either as the new ruling noble of the area.... or a Mage Kinain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:46:22-07:00","id":900318,"title":"","content":"The Fall, Ink, and the Imaginarium of Doctor Parnassus are all very much Changeling to me both Stylistically and in terms of Story.<br /> <br /> The Anime Puella Magi Madoka Magica while not properly the same thing in terms of story is very Much Changeling in terms of Visual Elements. The Abilities of the Magical Girls seem almost like Cantrips at times, they Live under a Dual Identity that begins to pull them apart from their Mortal Lives as time goes on, and The Witches...Oh The Witches. They remind me of Very Powerful and Dangerous Chimera as well as Changelings that have become Entirely Freehold Bound in the most terrifying cases of Bedlam, Their Labyrinths are very Surreal as well, taking an entirely different animation style from the main show creating very Unique and Disturbing Visuals that reflect the Inner Psyche of the Witch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T23:53:10-07:00","id":901816,"title":"","content":"In the vein of <b>Millennium Actress</b> I would suggest the predecessor, <b>Perfect Blue</b>, which shows a very Unseelie side of Japanese Stardom and often blurs the line between reality and fantasy. Her sister is very much a Dauntain who had her dreams shattered only to end up in Bedlam after (without spoiling much) QUICKLY shedding Banality.<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest the <b>Tecmo's Deception</b> video games, well, #2 (Kagero: Deception) and the interestingly named Nightmare Princess (technically a remix of the 6th game of the series). Ignore the demonic aspects and instead replace Hell/Darkworld with Arcadia and imagine the Princesses as Fae being forced to work for their Unseelie nature (I like to imagine them as Leanhaun). Without spoiling more (check out some let's plays, if you don't like the series it isn't worth buying) the Velguirie route is PERFECT for playing or portraying a Typhoid Dauntain dragging people into their infectious glamour.<br /> <br /> And, while not perfect, <b>The Babadook</b> is a lot, to me, like a Childling coming out of their Chrysalis and forcing their parent into the role of a Grump or reluctant Kinain.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, depending on your taste for camp and kitsch, check out RuPaul's Drag Race. The transformation from male to glamourous or shockingly female can be pretty amazing and like the mortal vs. the fae. Plus seeing how meek some of the men are as men compared to how together and animated they are in drag is pretty interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Debating between ghouls and hunters PbP","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11874-melora","name":"Melora","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T19:05:21-07:00","id":903185,"title":"","content":"Mery Poppins<br /> Malificent<br /> Return to Neverland<br /> The Halloween tree<br /> <br /> ....i been thinking a lot about this one but.... A Goofy Movie.. a kid learning to grow up and also coping with his father's insanity? to live both in the real world and in the world of impossible things with his father?... sounds pretty changeling to me<br /> <br /> <br /> As for videogames..<br /> American Mcgee's alice ?<br /> <br /> <br /> any chances to stick this thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:39:00-07:00","id":911825,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping we'll get to add American Gods to the list... someday","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T00:55:04-07:00","id":917855,"title":"","content":"Finding Neverland both the film and Broadway show","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T00:51:00-07:00","id":931232,"title":"","content":"A Midsummer Night's Dream! Even more for Dark Ages: Fae.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T06:35:28-07:00","id":931319,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised that no one brought up <b>Song of the Sea </b>yet. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VrhoOzW8oF8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VrhoOzW8oF8</a> [Trailer on YouTube)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7erpJFZhvTU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7erpJFZhvTU</a> [US Trailer]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":2494,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","user":"Rigistrade","date":". 07-14-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T07:49:09-07:00","id":931352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rigistrade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=931319#post931319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that no one brought up <b>Song of the Sea </b>yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>How did I not know that existed? I must see it now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T23:54:19-07:00","id":931859,"title":"","content":"Several Robin Williams movies have already been mentioned - not surprising, since so many of his favorite themes echo those of <i>Changeling</i>. <b>Toys</b> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cP-TU0P2Lw4\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>) is definitely worth a mention, too. <br /> <br /> If you want crossover ideas, though, take a look at <b>What Dreams May Come </b>(<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TPZpQsEFcKI\" target=\"_blank\"><u>trailer</u></a>), which plays out like a romance between a wraith and a changeling. The roles swap about hallway, though. A wraith mourns his lost love, even has he waits for her in the Dreaming. And a changeling plums the depths of the Labyrinth, looking for the wraith of his beloved. <br /> <br /> Even if you don't like the movie plotline, you can pull a number of setting ideas (for both game lines)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drazosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=876711#post876711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . Lost Girl also has some value. Particularly, the way their Seelie and Unseelie equivalents interact, and the way those courts aren't purely good or evil in stereotypical ways, can come in handy for more social games. The character of Kenzi also makes a great example of an Enchanted mortal ally. Some of the monsters they fight can also make decent inspiration for Gallain, rogue chimera, or adhene. As a warning, the show is a bit adult, and some episodes can definitely be a bit monster-of-the-week, but it's a fun fae-focused romp if you don't take it too seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good series. Good suggestion, too<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T20:57:08-07:00","id":932370,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Robin William's, there's a Terry Gilliam movie he's in called The Fisher King. Speaking of Terry Gilliam, there's Time Bandits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T19:45:57-07:00","id":986526,"title":"","content":"From an earlier post I made on this subject:<br /> Sundae, a short story read aloud. From Pod Castle. Despite the complete absence of faeries, this story says Changeling to me more than any other. It's dark, and epic and mythical all at once. The story of a teddy bear made to protect children from the dark horrors of night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://podcastle.org/2013/04/03/podcastle-254-sundae/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://podcastle.org/wp-content/themes/escape-artists-base-theme/images/ea.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://podcastle.org/2013/04/03/podcastle-254-sundae/\" target=\"_blank\"> PodCastle 254: Sundae - PodCastle </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://podcastle.org/2013/04/03/podcastle-254-sundae/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://podcastle.org/2013/04/03/podcastle-254-sundae/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sundae by Matt Wallace Perhaps the greatest warrior the world had ever known was entombed in a brown cardboard box in the attic. The box was scrawled &ldquo;Kenny&rsquo;s Room&rdquo; in bright red Sharpie pen and stuffed into a dust-covered corner one Spring-cleaning with several others. Some contained toys the children had outgrown, others contained electronics [&hellip;] </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7861-strafe","name":"Strafe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:28:17-08:00","id":1010821,"title":"","content":"Ok i think im HIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIGH...but listen up.<br /> <br /> Band of musicians inspire an entire country, they are suddenly kidnapped by an Evil Force who uses their music to keep himself alive and dry them out. One Heroe goes in the search of this band and his personal muse in a far lands of...........Planet Earth.<br /> <br /> IS INTERESTELLA: THE 5TORY OF THE 5ECRET 5TAR 5YSTEM by Daft Punk and Toei NOT a Changeling inspiration?! change the word &quot;Alien&quot; for Fae and i think youre prettty much there.<br /> <br /> And for those who dont know what im talking about.. Here go some of the music videos that make the movie<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-OTryGzS-G8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-OTryGzS-G8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-OTryGzS-G8 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-OTryGzS-G8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-OTryGzS-G8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L93-7vRfxNs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L93-7vRfxNs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L93-7vRfxNs </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L93-7vRfxNs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L93-7vRfxNs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FxzBvqY5PP0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"