l to Earth&quot; consider as Changeling material? / the story of Ziggy Stardust","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-10-2017, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T09:10:27-08:00","id":1030083,"title":"","content":"Would Alice Madness Returns be a good example of the breakdown of a quimerical reality because of a Winter Person?<br /> <br /> Also... i cant stop thinking of changelings fighting Emotional Baggage so...<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MqTrdptLRrs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MqTrdptLRrs</a> ? or would fit more as a mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T03:13:28-08:00","id":1032062,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Dirk Gently could be a good inspiration for an eshu detective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T15:53:09-08:00","id":1032356,"title":"","content":"I'm growing really fond of Pixar-style movies for dreamscape inspirations. Inside Out is just amazing, and with a little tweaking The Secret Life of Pets could be adapted to what domestic chimera do when their changelings aren't around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:04:16-08:00","id":1034362,"title":"","content":"I'm a little sad that no one has mentioned Emma Bull's War of the Oaks. <br /> <br /> Also, Megan Lindholm's Wizard of the Pigeons. <br /> <br /> Charles de Lint's Jack the Giant Killer and Yarrow: An Autumn Tale.<br /> <br /> Ray Bradbury's Something Wicked This Way Comes.<br /> <br /> Simon R. Green's Drinking Midnight Wine.<br /> <br /> Orson Scott Card's Magic Street. Also The Lost Gate. <br /> <br /> The original Nightmare on Elm Street and Clive Barker's Candyman (about an urban legend that is trying to become real). (Yes, my take on Changeling tends to be a wee bit darker than most.)<br /> <br /> And Labyrinth. I always liked the film but gained a new appreciation of it when Lea Sheppard (IIRC) pointed out that any time Sarah does what a character in a fairy tale would do, she fails, only succeeding when she doesn't do what a fairy tale character would, and when she takes the fairy tale route in her final confrontation with the Goblin King, the look on David Bowie's face is one of pure disappointment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:15:33-08:00","id":1034612,"title":"","content":"Theres a Neil Gaiman Short story called &quot;The Return of the Thin White Duke.&quot; you guys should read it asap","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T21:17:05-08:00","id":1038261,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0A6500g-QWY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0A6500g-QWY</a> i recently saw this trailer..if this is noit good media inspiration for changeling, then i dont know what a fuck it is","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T11:15:29-08:00","id":1049948,"title":"","content":"I've got several pieces of inspiration that I look toward when preparing a Changeling story, but none have so recently stirred the imagination quite as well as:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Gortimer-Gibbons-Life-Normal-Street/dp/B00I3MOU4Y\" target=\"_blank\">Gortimer Gibbons Life on Normal Street</a> -- </i>follows Gortimer and his two best friends, Ranger and Mel, on magical exploits triggered by their thirst for adventure. The trio sets out to end a jinx while helping the unluckiest kid on Normal Street, solve a mystery before a spooky spirit turns them into ghost stories, find a fabled lost treasure, and outsmart fate after some advice from a fortune teller.</div> <br /> Here are a few pieces that we LOVE for Changeling inspiration. They're a little darker, and they aren't literally Changeling--don't expect to see characters having a tea party with a wyvern--but if you were to video a bunch of Changelings in their lives using mundane camera, it might look a little something like these.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> An unseelie freehold on the bad side of town, owned by a satyr/sidhe sibling duo, and run with their rat-pooka and gay satyr friend gets bought out by the siblings' father, an old boggart grump. The gang goes about ravaging and spreading reverie across their town, clashing with other motleys and mortals, frequently teetering on the cusp of Bedlam. Despite their wild dispositions, dangerous shenanigans and often bleak lives, they can always take hope in the fact that <a href=\"http://www.fxnetworks.com/shows/its-always-sunny-in-philadelphia\" target=\"_blank\">It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia</a>.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Of a similar vane, (Possibly even a continuation?) but much closer to home, the unseelie satyr aunt of a noble family shows up to a party--just as the Count and Countess are found to be Oathbreakers and flee their small holdings, leaving their three children behind! The aunt deals with the family, doing the best that a commoner can do to hold together a noble seelie family. She faces a whole host of struggles and misadventures as she tries to cope with her sidhe niece growing into a wilder, while struggling to find her footing with her redcap and nocker nephews, leaning heavily on the house's generous boggan nanny to keep things running. Completely out of her element, <a href=\"http://www.fox.com/the-mick\" target=\"_blank\">The Mick</a> does her best to deal with mortal and kithain high society while keeping her family's legacy together (at least for herself.)</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13012,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13012-rampagingsnark","user":"rampagingsnark","date":". 02-16-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13012-rampagingsnark","name":"rampagingsnark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T08:34:57-08:00","id":1051532,"title":"","content":"You guys have got to listen to the podcast <a href=\"http://www.orbitinghumancircus.com/podcast.html\" target=\"_blank\">Orbiting Human Circus (of the Air)</a>. It is so Changeling it hurts. <br /> <br /> After hearing OHC, I'm considering adding a chimerical Narrator to all my chronicles from now on. (A disembodied voice, that basically means that the characters can hear me.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T07:51:39-08:00","id":1052005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GogariGlenRoss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=1051532#post1051532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm considering adding a chimerical Narrator to all my chronicles from now on. (A disembodied voice, that basically means that the characters can hear me.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was inspired by Pushing Daisies and Princess Tutu to have a narrator in a chronicle once. The plan was that the narrator was actually a Tuatha de Danaan who came back to check in how the Kithain were doing as stewards of the Dreaming. It was going to faithfully narrate the first couple of sessions, then audibly get more frustrated by what it considered poor story choices by the PCs as the chronicle went on, eventually getting fed up and taking more direct control of events going on around the characters. The PCs would have to find a way to break free from the Tuatha's script.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, shortly into the chronicle, several players' life situations changed, so it had to be abandoned before we got to the reveal of the Tuatha de Danaan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:19:14-08:00","id":1052316,"title":"","content":"I forget, has anyone mentioned Clive Barker's The Thief of Always or Weaveworld? Or Stephen King's IT or his and Peter Straud's The Talisman? (Admittedly, they may skew a little more Lost than Dreaming, but are all worth reading.)<br /> <br /> Also, I'm sort of enjoying the new show Emerald City. Not as much as some of the other stuff I watch, but visually it's very fascinating. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:01:18-08:00","id":1052591,"title":"","content":"I thought the recent Channel Zero: Candle Cove series made for an interesting mine of Changeling material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:19:09-08:00","id":1055755,"title":"","content":"The &quot;White Walkers&quot; from Game of Thrones, not exactly CtD, much more fitting for DA Fae, as some powerful changellings of the Winter Court. The very first time I saw the White Walkers I thought &quot;Winter Court&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:10:55-08:00","id":1059855,"title":"","content":"Ok. Imma drop this here but..Has anyone read the last Hellboy Arc?. No, not BPRD. Hellboy, where he basically summons the armies of Arthurian legend to fight Nimue, messenger and champion of The Dragon of Revelations?.<br /> <br /> because if thats not good inspiration for changeling, i have no idea what else might be<br /> <br /> <br /> ALSO..Would Alan Wake be a good example of changeling? from the point of view of an Enchanted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 03-07-2017, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T13:42:00-08:00","id":1060256,"title":"","content":"All of Hellboy is wonderful inspiration just for the amounts of real world myth and folklore it's always drawn upon. My two personal favorites are his adventures in Mexico in the 50s and the one about the African legend of Makoma. <br /> <br /> You know, the Kingdom of the Feathered Serpent should really have some sort of heroic knightly order who are all masked luchadors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T17:50:27-07:00","id":1062569,"title":"","content":"So, i been reading this novel by Joe Hill &quot;NOS4A2&quot; About a child killer who takes them to a place known as &quot;ChristmasLand.&quot;<br /> The protagonist (Vic) has this &quot;Gift&quot; which allows her to ride her bicycle and teleport Anywhere where she wants to (by crossing an imaginaty bridge)<br /> <br /> (BY THE WAY, TO AVOID SPOILERS. THE FIRST 5 PAGES STABLISH THAT THE KILLER'S BEEN IN A COMA FOR DECADES, THE BOOK IS NARRATED THROUGH FLASHBACKS AND FLASHFOWARDS).<br /> <br /> Vic was able to &quot;Escape&quot; manx (The Killer) when she was very young. The book potraits her &quot;Teleporting&quot; to his home.<br /> In the current page where i am, she is describing having &quot;Two Version&quot; of how she got there in her mind. One being that she ran away from home, tried to take a train, Charles Manx (The killer) poisoned her and took her to his Car (Which for any purpouses could be a Chimera) and took her to the house on &quot;Christmas land.&quot; (an abandoned themepark). The other version is that she heard about him through a librarian who can get &quot;Clues&quot; by throwing pices from Scabble, she took her bike and went through the Imaginary Bridge, and she ended up on this old house smelling of Gingerbread and with Dead Childrens/Demonic Kids/Kidnapped children..<br /> <br /> So....<br /> <br /> Is it a good inspiration for Changeling or am i High Again?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T14:36:05-07:00","id":1062977,"title":"","content":"NOS4A2 is a little more Lost than Dreaming (IMO), but still a good read, and does offer up some interesting ideas for darker corners of the Dreaming. I was rather amused by the book's map showing ChristmasLand also including references to Hill's earlier book Horns and his graphic novel series Lock &amp; Key, as well as to his father's book IT. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T11:56:20-07:00","id":1078450,"title":"","content":"I was about to suggest Astrid Lindgren's story, very befitting of Changeling in theme and tone, but couldn't find any evidence of it ever translated into English. In Swedish it's called &quot;Junker Nins av Eka&quot; (<a href=\"http://www.astridlindgren.se/en/her-works/books/character/junker-nils\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.astridlindgren.se/en/her-...er/junker-nils</a>).<br /> <br /> But if you read Swedish or any of the languages it was translated in (like Russian), I'd put it on as recommended reading. <br /> <br /> Firkraag's out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T04:04:43-07:00","id":1078826,"title":"","content":"If your looking for ideas for Australian Changelings you can't go too far wrong with The Song of Wirrun trilogy and other books like The Nargun and the Stars<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/3267262-the-song-of-wirrun\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1246809194i/3267262.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/3267262-the-song-of-wirrun\" target=\"_blank\"> The Song of Wirrun: Ice is Coming, Dark Bright Water an&hellip; </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/3267262-the-song-of-wirrun\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/3267262-the-song-of-wirrun </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Discover and share books you love on Goodreads. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:11:07-07:00","id":1086968,"title":"","content":"Clive Barker, <i>The Thief of Always. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T19:14:55-07:00","id":1088590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maggie C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=1086968#post1086968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clive Barker, <i>The Thief of Always. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough...I feel like Doctor Who has some very changeling elements and episodes. i mean the whole thing of 11th being amy's &quot;Imaginary friend.&quot;<br /> Episodes like &quot;Blink&quot;, The Hotel One (11th), just to name a few.. but tell me if im Off my meds again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:57:29-07:00","id":1088992,"title":"","content":"It's not really a good match tonally, but I've thought the television show Grimm made for good inspiration on ways to look at chimerical reality vs. regular reality, and how to use it with adult characters that all share this layer of culture and society that isn't perceived by many ordinary people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T12:13:35-07:00","id":1089305,"title":"","content":"<i>Shade: The Changing Man</i>, from DC's Vertigo imprint back in the 90s. <br /> <br /> Rudyard Kipling's <i>Puck of Pook's Hill</i><br /> <br /> China Mieville's <i>King Rat</i><br /> <br /> Helene Wecker's <i>The Golem and the Jinni</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T12:58:11-07:00","id":1091235,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r2pt2-F2j2g\" target=\"_blank\">This movie</a></b>. </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Willy Wonka &amp; the Chocolate Factory</span></span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I think this has to be a Freehold of the Lost Ones. And you know the owner is mad. As <i>Nostalgia Critic</i> put it:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>&quot;He has the ideas and ambition of a child yet the mind and demeanor of a James Bond villain.&quot;</i></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-11-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T17:50:30-07:00","id":1091351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=1091235#post1091235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willy Wonka &amp; the Chocolate Factory</div> </div> </div> </div>All of Roald Dahl's books make for good Changeling reading. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T18:07:13-07:00","id":1091358,"title":"","content":"Partial to 'Harvey' myself. Both the Jimmy Stewart and Harry Anderson versions are good...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1666-firstborn8","name":"Firstborn8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:03:30-07:00","id":1092379,"title":"","content":"Miss Kobyashi's Dragon Maid. Honestly this is what i think its like to be Enchanted/Kinain. Its very tonnally lite and silly and well about dragons but how the human characters lives are made more interesting while they still handle a regular life to allow their dragon friends to go off and have crazy adventures seems perfect for getting across the situation between Kithain and those on the edge.<br /> <br /> Also you could do worse than looking at Kana for Childling inspiration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:12:00-07:00","id":1092449,"title":"","content":"Might be useful:<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J2se_zimj40\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">African Pantheons and the Orishas</span></span></a></span></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:43:31-07:00","id":1092552,"title":"","content":"There is a great children's series called Geronimo Stilton and the Kingdom of Fantasy. Mild mannered busy body mouse is suddenly taken to another realm of high fantasy and must overcome his own failings and help the people of the realm. My kid got into this one and so I was drawn in too. The Thomas Covenant Chronicles is an adult version. With books the genre of fantasy is rife with series about the things Changeling is trying to reclaim. I'm not really into the modern stuff so I wouldn't know much that would completely mirror the duality aspect.<br /> <br /> Adventure Time and the Amazing World of Gumball are great childling primers. The episode of AWoG about the board game Dodge or Dare is great.<br /> <br /> Music...Avantasia the Metal Opera 1&amp;2 by Tobias Sammet.<br /> <br /> The Lego Movie, Secondhand Lions.... There are honestly lots of fantasy themed movies that work better for the Dreaming aspect of the game. Too numerous to list. There are lots that hit on the duality or hiding what you are aspect. In Dreams is a favorite of mine. Not really a close corollary, but I could see lines that can be drawn.<br /> <br /> Has no one mentioned Stranger Things?<br /> <br /> The Fifth Element is a bit of a reach. But if you see Dallas as a retired Troll or House Scathach Sidhe who takes up a cause to help a newly returned Sidhe sorceress to prevent the Elder Dark from returning, Zerg being a House Balor seeking the return with the help of a group of Troll/Ogre/Redcaps and the setting being either the future or the Dreaming...then you might see where I'm coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","user":"KyleFianna","date":". 05-15-2017, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T03:30:46-07:00","id":1092718,"title":"","content":"There is another series I forgot. Fablehaven by Brandon Mull. A secret nature reserve for the world's mythical/legendary creatures. Everything has to behave according to laws set forth in a treaty of sorts. Some grandchildren of the caretaker arrive when parents leave on a vacation and discover their grandfather is running this magically protected place of wonder.<br /> <br /> Of course if it wasn't mentioned before Spiderwick Chronicles are there too.... You even get more of Tony DiTerlizzi's badass artwork.<br /> <br /> Granted both of those have us normies discovering the fantastic world instead of being born into the life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T23:55:41-07:00","id":1094444,"title":"","content":"I didnt mention the Anime Berserk. If you can find the original series from the 90s it is way better. They revived it as a concise three movie dvd and subsequently it is now a serial detailing the events in the Manga. Both the 90s series and the recent 3 dvd release are a prelude. The premise is heavily influenced by events from medieval Europe and is perfect for Dreaming heavy or modern settings that want to focus more on the Fae side of things. The current series is more of a Nightmare influenced setting, almost the Elder Darks won sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","user":"KyleFianna","date":". 05-19-2017, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13418-kylefianna","name":"KyleFianna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T00:12:19-07:00","id":1094447,"title":"","content":"Paranoid Agent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:39:07-07:00","id":1095285,"title":"","content":"Cornelia Funke's <i>Inkheart</i>, if no one has mentioned it already. And whichever books from Jim Butcher's <i>Dresdon Files</i> that deal primarily with the Fey Courts (<i>Summer Knight</i> and <i>Cold Days</i>, IIRC).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T23:56:11-07:00","id":1095778,"title":"","content":"the comic book Fables, would it work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Cha