 dream to become an anthropomorfic personification?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:19:36-07:00","id":1099258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=1098647#post1098647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I been curious about running a game mixing American Gods, Fables and Nos4a2. but i wonder if (to make them fit in the changeling lore) is it possible for a dream to become an anthropomorfic personification?</div> </div> </div> </div>My instinct would be to say, &quot;yes&quot;. I'm just unsure of what rule-related things - Backgrounds, merits, etc. - would be necessary to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T16:19:06-07:00","id":1100252,"title":"","content":"...IM CALLING IT!. Edgar Wright's Spaced. specially on the fingershootout scene and the Paintball match....and also Comunity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T01:49:10-07:00","id":1100372,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was mentionned but I've just finished it and it was gorgeous. I'm talking of Child of Light. It's like you're playing a childing Sidhe in a quest to save a Dreaming Realm from an Unseelie Queen. I mean, even the clans can be seen as kith in Changeling, the Aerostati being pixies, the Capilli being boggans and so on...<br /> If you haven't played it yet, I recommend it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T04:49:30-07:00","id":1102234,"title":"","content":"For BOOKS I would reccommend:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Which-Witch-Eva-Ibbotson/dp/0141304278/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1497376628&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Which+Witch+by+Eva+Ibbotson\" target=\"_blank\">Which Witch</a> by Eva Ibbotson (The spellcasters here are more like changelings and kinain that Mages)<br /> <br /> The Dark is Rising by Susan Cooper (already mentioned)<br /> <br /> The Neverending Story (Already mentioned, but important)<br /> <br /> Dreams Underfoot Collection by Charles DeLint<br /> <br /> What the Cat Told Me by Diana Wynne Jones (short story)<br /> <br /> Not What You Expected by Joan Aiken (shorts stories, all of which are suitable for Changeling)<br /> <br /> The Last Unicorn by Peter S. Beagel (fae vs mortal seeming is a big theme)<br /> <br /> The Big Over Easy by Jasper Fforde (Fairy Tale and Mythic beings living in a modern world)<br /> <br /> The Mythology Series by Jodi Lynn Nye<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Changeling-Delia-Sherman/dp/0142411884/ref=tmm_pap_swatch_0?_encoding=UTF8&amp;qid=&amp;sr=\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> by Delia Sherman<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Five-Children-Puffin-Classics-Nesbit/dp/014132161X/ref=sr_1_3?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1497376549&amp;sr=1-3&amp;keywords=%E2%80%8BFive+Children+and+It+By+E.+Nesbit\" target=\"_blank\">Five Children and It</a> by E. Nesbit (anything by Nesbit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-13-2017, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T07:33:23-07:00","id":1102803,"title":"","content":"Fun movies with a fairy tale/Changeling vibe:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rZyVnXe3yV8\" target=\"_blank\">JORDSKOTT</a>- A Story about a community that is hiding the presence of a terrible evil (likely Thallain)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eQ4chNKBHOc\" target=\"_blank\">THALE </a>(modern, creepy take on the Huldra idea)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WhGFwk58h34\" target=\"_blank\">TROLL HUNTER</a> (found footage, really wonderful)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9RQlikX4vvw\" target=\"_blank\">RARE EXPORTS</a> (kid hero, goes someplace I didn't expect - creepy and fun)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:00:20-08:00","id":1178958,"title":"","content":"*creaks open door to thread*<br /> <br /> Nobody here? Alright then.<br /> <br /> Anyways, this movie trailer dropped today, &quot;I Kill Giants&quot; (based on the comic mini-series &quot;I Kill Giants&quot;), and it's the most goddamn Changeling thing I've seen to come out of 2018 thus far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IkkFNPbRQ0\" data-code=\"6IkkFNPbRQ0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6IkkFNPbRQ0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> A childling changeling (rabbit ears would suggest pooka) fights and kills chimerical giants and naturally nobody believes here when she talks about how the giants are real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 01-25-2018, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:18:27-08:00","id":1178968,"title":"","content":"Happy! is a TV series on SCIFI about an Excop crushed by the world who has become a hit man.. who teams up with an imaginary friend of a little girl to save her. This alone is pretty weird but the whole setting has an odd undercurrent of &quot;What hte fuck is really going on&quot; that could be &quot;this is how mortals see changeling&quot; interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T20:08:54-08:00","id":1179068,"title":"","content":"If this hasn't been suggested already, I say Bridge to Terabithia is right on the money for Changeling, the Dreaming. In fact, as soon as I heard about the concept and setting of the game, I immediately thought of BtT.<br /> <br /> Couple of kids want to escape from their problems in the real world, so they go exploring in the woods and find a place where they can just hang out by themselves for hours without anybody bothering them. Shortly afterward, they name the spot Terabithia and imagine a fantasy world filled with magical creatures and grand adventures!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T2TDSEG57hI\" data-code=\"T2TDSEG57hI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/T2TDSEG57hI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T15:10:21-08:00","id":1179320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/861056-good-media-inspiration-for-changeling?p=1178958#post1178958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*creaks open door to thread*<br /> <br /> Nobody here? Alright then.<br /> <br /> Anyways, this movie trailer dropped today, &quot;I Kill Giants&quot; dropped today (based on the comic mini-series &quot;I Kill Giants&quot;), and it's the most goddamn Changeling thing I've seen to come out of 2018 thus far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IkkFNPbRQ0\" data-code=\"6IkkFNPbRQ0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6IkkFNPbRQ0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> A childling changeling (rabbit ears would suggest pooka) fights and kills chimerical giants and naturally nobody believes here when she talks about how the giants are real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, finally a trailer! Eagerly waiting for this one, I loved the comic. <br /> <br /> I can attest that, without spoiling much, it works perfectly as inspiration for Changeling","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T06:42:58-08:00","id":1182246,"title":"","content":"The Adventures of Baron Munchausen. You literally have a guy who loses his memory and youth as he alternates between giving in to normalcy and death and remembering how he's a fantastical hero of myth and legend. Your not even sure what is real and what is just a story of the Baron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T09:44:23-08:00","id":1182634,"title":"","content":"I have a few video games to offer:<br /> THIEF: The Dark Project (the original. It's about an elder fae trying to stop their sundering.)<br /> Contrast (a girl and her chimera of her making are trying to understand the world from the shadows of her freehold)<br /> Costume Quest (Just play it!)<br /> Guns of Icarus (Kinda kidding... though I do like the ideas of Knockers just going on it in airships!) <br /> Five Nights at Freddy's 4... NO! Seriously! This is probably the perfect representation of what an a childling goes through when they are being besieged by their own nocnista and have only a glamour-loaded flashlight to protect themselves. It has nightmare logic, grotesque monstrosities and all you need is the monsters leaving to cause carnage in the nearby freeholds.<br /> Shower with your Dad Simulator (Ok, I'm REALLY kidding with that one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T21:41:15-08:00","id":1182806,"title":"","content":"...<br /> <br /> South Park the Stick of Truth maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T21:55:30-08:00","id":1182811,"title":"","content":"Also. i been reading a lot of the discworld lately and started to read Saga. they mention the idea of the Narrative Laws of Causality.<br /> <br /> basically saying, that if its worth of an epic tale. it will happend.<br /> If an army has to fight 7 heroes, the army will loose.<br /> <br /> i can't stop thinking on using that law on my games..except when it comes to banality <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TheoryOfNarrativeCausality\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...ativeCausality</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T20:07:44-08:00","id":1184211,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VR8wXsvUrBg\" target=\"_blank\">American Mcgee's Alice</a> is a great example.<br /> <br /> In fact, if you use both games as inspiration, Alice could be an example of a playable Dauntain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-10-2018, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T22:48:37-08:00","id":1184635,"title":"","content":"Ok i got a curve ball...<br /> <br /> Would &quot;Once upon a time&quot;/&quot;The Wolf Among us&quot; be good inspiration for changeling?<br /> <br /> for a while i been pondering of how to run a game where my PC's are actually fable's characters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T02:36:04-08:00","id":1184669,"title":"","content":"Once upon a time works well to give several examples on how Mists work and how frustrating it can get. Seriously few first seasons get extremely frustrating at times as the main character refuses to believe no matter what she witnessess and tends to forget the things she just saw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T16:08:35-08:00","id":1529177,"title":"","content":"A few movies that came out since this topic was started:<br /> <b>Christopher Robin</b> 2018<br /> <b>The Kid Who Would Be King</b> 2019<br /> <b>Slumberland</b> 2022<br /> <br /> The latter is on Netflix, the former two on Disney+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T18:02:55-08:00","id":1529265,"title":"","content":"If you want something unusual and unique for Nocker inspiration (and have a few hours), there is English prog rock band Gandalf's Fist and their album <i>The Clockwork Fable</i>. It's essentially a three disc rock opera/radio play about a subterranean steampunk city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T11:43:44-08:00","id":1531371,"title":"","content":"I can heartily recommend <b>Three Thousand Years of Longing</b> (2022). About the interaction between a Dreamer (Tilda Swinton) and an ancient fae (Idris Elba).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T09:41:06-08:00","id":1531475,"title":"","content":"It may not be obvious but IMHO &quot;Truman Show&quot; is a good example of incoming Chrysalis/First Change when the world is trying to bring you down. I would also add &quot;Dead Poet's Society&quot;, seeing Keating as an aging grump Boogan who tries to rejuvenate himself by mentoring a group of potential Fae. Also &quot;The Invention of Hugo Cabret&quot; and &quot;Golden Compass&quot;<br /> <br /> As for music &quot;Symphony for the Enchanted Lands&quot; by Rhapsody of Fire. I know, it may be clich\u00e9 but the story is great and I have trouble to imagine better OST for battle with the chimerical dragon.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T12:41:47-07:00","id":1539160,"title":"","content":"<b>The Imaginary</b> (2023) is an anime film very in line with CtD, but from the point of view of chimerae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T09:37:19-07:00","id":1539218,"title":"","content":"Shaolin Soccer (best watched with subtitles not dubbed) makes a lot more sense when you realise that most of the kung fu brothers are high banality changelings, with the exception of the one who is always trying to find ways to save them from banality's pull.<br /> <br /> In fact most soccer stars seem to be changelings in that film.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T09:42:15-07:00","id":1539219,"title":"","content":"Who Framed Roger Rabbit? is my go to movie for shamanism, but it has some elements that work well for changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T14:55:46-07:00","id":1539252,"title":"","content":"Chip n' Dale Rescue Rangers, the movie, it's very good at blending whimsy with heavy stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T13:28:54-07:00","id":1539337,"title":"","content":"In case anyone needs an example of how a Sidhe's Noble Bearing might make them be affected by a power differently from others, here's a short <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=htkUa_fVwCA\" target=\"_blank\">clip</a> from Doctor Who that illustrates it perfectly in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-18T07:41:53-07:00","id":1551753,"title":"","content":"The Dutch fairytale theme park Efteling:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5KfWFuHT3tQ\" data-code=\"5KfWFuHT3tQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5KfWFuHT3tQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Obviously most of the park has a CtD vibe. But of special interest for instance is the Droomvlucht (Dreamflight) dark ride. In it you fly through several (seemingly unconnected) scenes populated by fae creatures. Also one of the park's hotels is built to look like a flying castle with a steampunk engine room. Cause its back story is that powered by hotel guests' dreams it flies off at night to explore the magical realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T03:57:37-07:00","id":1551763,"title":"","content":"Look for a Russian film called <b>Upon the Magic Road.</b> It's based on <b>The Little Humpbacked Horse.</b> The visuals are amazing. I haven't gotten a chance to see the 2024 film, just excerpts, but the Russian literary fairy tale is great both for mood and the little horse is a great Chimeric friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}